  "lib": "RTFcredits",
  "num": 1,
  "name": "",
  "type": "field",
  "text": "READ\nME!\n\n\nCastmembers 11 and 12 of this castLib are rich-text (RTF) fields containing the scrolling credits used by the EXIT.DIR file. A separate version is provided for Mac and Windows so that platform-specific fonts and sizes can be used.\n\nYou can edit the credits simply by double-clicking the castmembers in the Cast window. This will open a rich-text window with basic word-processor features.\n\nTo change the color of selected text, open the Tool Palette window (Window menu > Tool Palette), and choose a color from the foreground color pop-up palette.\n\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThe background color of the text fields must remain black. Do not change this.\n\nThe field margin must remain at 5 inches.\n\nOnly use only standard System fonts that are known to be available on each platform.\n\nTry to avoid font sizes smaller than 12 points. These will not anti-alias and may become illegible on an overhead projection system.\n\n\n\n"
 },
